What this package is
--------------------

  * a structured paraphrase of the book's arguments, written in this package's own words, with
    page references so a reader can check every claim against the printed book;

  * an ERRATA REGISTER: the transcription defects, internal contradictions and numbering faults
    found while distilling the book are documented card by card, each with the page and, where
    possible, a recomputation that demonstrates the defect. This register is the package's own
    contribution;

  * a boundary statement: several of the book's chapters promise substantially more than they
    deliver, and the package says so rather than papering over it.


What this package is NOT
------------------------

  * it is not the book, and cannot substitute for it. Read the book;

  * it contains no verbatim passages. An automated audit against the source transcription found a
    longest shared run of zero characters across all cards; the few ten-character matches that
    remain are chapter titles, the book title, and parameter-name pairs used as table labels, all
    registered as structural exemptions;

  * all formulas are marked unchecked against the printed page, and all numbers are marked as
    transcription values.


